# Provenance of proto/SandboxContext.proto: vendored VERBATIM from
# apple/containerization at the ref below. Keep it byte-identical to upstream —
# unused RPCs/messages included — so the ancestry stays auditable.
#
# There is exactly one copy of the proto and one generated tree
# (internal/sandbox), imported by both the host client (pkg/guest) and the guest
# server (guest/internal/guestagent), so no cross-copy sync check is needed: regenerate
# with `just proto`.
#
# Ossein's OWN RPCs live in proto/Ossein.proto, a separate file and service
# (OsseinGuest) generated into the same Go package. That split is what keeps this
# pledge honest: anything ossein needs and upstream lacks goes there, so
# SandboxContext.proto never has to be edited and its ancestry stays auditable.
#
# The initfs is NOT covered by this pin: ossein owns the guest (guest/vminitd) and
# builds initfs.ext4 in-repo. Host↔guest compatibility is enforced at runtime by
# the protocol-revision handshake, and every constant the two ends must agree on
# (revision, its env var, the vsock port, the initfs init path) is declared ONCE
# in internal/protocol and imported by both — so bumping the revision is one edit,
# not two kept in step.
